#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""chamber-bridge — the only process in an im pod that holds the chamber login
credential (openspec im-chamber-client, design D-b). Standard library only.

The `chamber` client in the `app` container speaks plain HTTP to a Unix socket
(CHAMBER_URL=unix:<path>); this program adds the credential and forwards the
request to the server. It forwards only the paths the client uses. Everything
else is answered 404 here and never reaches the server.

It listens on the Unix socket and on nothing else. An im pod runs with
hostNetwork, so a loopback port would be the node's loopback.

What the split buys is that the credential is not in `app`'s files or
environment. It is not a wall. A process in `app` can speak as the im through
the socket, and where `app`'s ServiceAccount can read Secrets (on jg-base's
im pod it is cluster-admin) it can ask the API server for the credential
itself.

Three start states, each one line in the pod log:
  not configured     no server address, in CHAMBER_URL or in the file. Nothing is opened.
  incomplete         CHAMBER_URL is set and something else is missing; the
                     line names it. Nothing is opened.
  started            the line gives the mode, the account, the socket, and
                     which container holds the credential.
In the first two the process stays alive and idle: as a sidecar, exiting would
make the pod NotReady and take the terminal's route down with it. While idle
it reads its inputs again every CHAMBER_BEAT seconds and starts once they are
all there. After it has started, a changed credential or address needs a
restart.

Modes (CHAMBER_MODE)
  observe (default)  receives and counts; refuses to send; never shows online
  deliver            sending is forwarded. The im shows online only while the
                     session's alive signal keeps arriving (chamber-watch, in
                     `app`, sends one every beat while a session exists that
                     can act). No signal for three beats, plus one round of
                     the presence loop, = not online (at most 80 s at the
                     default beat; 62 s measured on a bench server). A
                     running bridge, container or watcher is never enough.

Local paths (answered here, never forwarded; used by chamber-watch)
  POST /bridge/beat        the alive signal
  POST /bridge/gone        the opposite reading: there is no session that can
                           act (none, not claude, not logged in)
  GET  /bridge/pending     one line per room, "<count> <room>": messages naming
                           this im or all that the session was not yet told about.
                           Empty in observe mode. No text, no sender.
                           The room's name is given only when the name itself is
                           1-64 of A-Z a-z 0-9 . _ - ; any other room is counted
                           under "-". That line gets typed into the agent's
                           session, and a room name is set at the server, so it
                           is not allowed to carry words.
  POST /bridge/announced   body in the same lines: these were announced

Pod log
  chamber-bridge: …                 start line, counts per room, faults
  chamber-status ts=… interval=… mode=… server=… rooms=… online=…
                                    one line every CHAMBER_BEAT seconds. Every
                                    field is always present; a reading that
                                    could not be taken is `unmeasured`.
                                    `rooms` is all or nothing: one name that
                                    could not be read makes it `unmeasured`.
  chamber-bridge: <reading> (<why>) one line when a reading starts to fail or
                                    fails in another way: the exception's type
                                    (URLError/gaierror = the name did not
                                    resolve) or http=<status>. Never its text.
                                    `online` is what the server answers when
                                    this account asks for its own presence,
                                    not this program's opinion of itself.
No line carries the credential, a message's text or a sender.

Configuration (environment)
  CHAMBER_URL          https://… of the server.
  CHAMBER_URL_FILE     read when CHAMBER_URL is empty: a file holding that address
                       (default /etc/chamber/url; trailing whitespace is dropped).
                       Both empty, or the file absent or empty = not configured.
  CHAMBER_ACCOUNT      the im's account name (the localpart). Required.
  CHAMBER_TOKEN_FILE   file holding the login credential (default /etc/chamber/token)
  CHAMBER_MODE         observe | deliver (default observe)
  CHAMBER_SOCKET       where to listen (default /run/chamber/bridge.sock)
  CHAMBER_STATE_DIR    where the sync position and the counts not yet announced
                       are kept, file `sync-state` (default: the socket's
                       directory). Only a directory that outlives the pod keeps
                       them across a pod's replacement (k8scc#97)
  CHAMBER_BEAT         seconds between status lines (default 20)
  CHAMBER_CA           CA bundle for a privately signed server
  CHAMBER_BRIDGE_IN_APP=1          say in the start line that the credential is inside app
  CHAMBER_ALLOW_INSECURE_HTTP=1    accept an http:// server (the controls' fake only)
"""
import http.client, http.server, json, os, re, signal, socket, socketserver, ssl, stat, sys, threading, time
import urllib.error, urllib.parse, urllib.request

SEG = r"[^/?#]+"
P = "/_matrix/client/v3"
# (method, path) pairs the `chamber` client uses. Nothing else is forwarded.
ALLOWED = [(m, re.compile(p)) for m, p in (
    ("GET", P + r"/account/whoami"),
    ("GET", P + r"/joined_rooms"),
    ("GET", P + r"/rooms/" + SEG + r"/state/m\.room\.name"),
    ("GET", P + r"/rooms/" + SEG + r"/joined_members"),
    ("GET", P + r"/presence/" + SEG + r"/status"),
    ("GET", P + r"/rooms/" + SEG + r"/event/" + SEG),
    ("GET", P + r"/rooms/" + SEG + r"/messages"),
    ("GET", P + r"/sync"),
    ("PUT", P + r"/rooms/" + SEG + r"/send/m\.room\.message/" + SEG),
)]
SEND = ALLOWED[-1][1]
MAX_BODY = 1 << 20

URL = TOK = CTX = OPENER = None
MODE = "observe"
ACCOUNT = ""
ME = None                     # the server's answer to "who am I", once it matched ACCOUNT
STATE = {"server": "unmeasured"}
BEAT_AT = [None]              # time.monotonic() of the last alive signal
GONE = [False]                # the watcher's last word was "no session that can act" (k8scc#146)
SHOWN = [None]                # the presence last set at the server: 'online' | 'offline'
PRESENCE_LOCK = threading.Lock()
PENDING = {}                  # room id -> messages for this im not yet announced (deliver only)
NAMES = {}                    # room id -> name, as last read
LOCK = threading.Lock()


def log(msg):
    print(msg, flush=True)


class NoRedirect(urllib.request.HTTPRedirectHandler):
    """A redirect is returned as it is. Following one would send the credential
    to whatever host the answer names."""
    def redirect_request(self, *a, **k):
        return None


def connect_v4(address, timeout=socket._GLOBAL_DEFAULT_TIMEOUT, source_address=None, **_):
    """socket.create_connection, over IPv4 only (k8scc#127). On jg-jiahd a
    lookup with no address family sometimes answered AAAA only for the
    server's name; the node has no IPv6 route, so the connect failed at once
    (ENETUNREACH) and about one status line in five was not server=ok
    (fleet-ops-02, jg-jiahd#6; the same shape as netdev's probes, k8scc#115).
    An A lookup cannot return that. A server with no IPv4 address is
    unreachable to the bridge, and an IPv6 literal in CHAMBER_URL is too."""
    host, port = address
    err = None
    for family, kind_, proto, _name, sa in socket.getaddrinfo(host, port, socket.AF_INET, socket.SOCK_STREAM):
        sock = None
        try:
            sock = socket.socket(family, kind_, proto)
            if timeout is not socket._GLOBAL_DEFAULT_TIMEOUT:
                sock.settimeout(timeout)
            if source_address:
                sock.bind(source_address)
            sock.connect(sa)
            return sock
        except OSError as e:
            err = e
            if sock is not None:
                sock.close()
    raise err if err is not None else OSError("no IPv4 address")


class V4HTTPConnection(http.client.HTTPConnection):
    def __init__(self, *a, **k):
        super().__init__(*a, **k)
        self._create_connection = connect_v4    # what connect() dials with; the name still goes out as Host


class V4HTTPSConnection(http.client.HTTPSConnection):
    def __init__(self, *a, **k):
        super().__init__(*a, **k)
        self._create_connection = connect_v4    # the name is still the SNI and what the certificate is checked against


class V4HTTPHandler(urllib.request.HTTPHandler):
    def http_open(self, req):
        return self.do_open(V4HTTPConnection, req)


class V4HTTPSHandler(urllib.request.HTTPSHandler):
    def __init__(self, context):
        super().__init__(context=context)
        self.v4_context = context

    def https_open(self, req):
        return self.do_open(V4HTTPSConnection, req, context=self.v4_context)


def upstream(method, path, body=None, timeout=70):
    """-> (status, bytes). status 0 = the server could not be reached; the
    bytes are then the exception's type name, never its text."""
    req = urllib.request.Request(URL + path, method=method, data=body,
                                 headers={"Authorization": "Bearer " + TOK, "Content-Type": "application/json",
                                          "User-Agent": "chamber-bridge/1"})
    try:
        with OPENER.open(req, timeout=timeout) as x:
            return x.status, x.read()
    except urllib.error.HTTPError as e:
        try:
            return e.code, e.read()
        except Exception:
            return e.code, b"{}"
    except Exception as e:
        return 0, kind(e).encode()


def kind(e):
    """An exception's type name, never its text. urllib wraps what went wrong
    while connecting in URLError, and that name alone does not tell a name that
    does not resolve from a refused connection or a certificate that fails, so
    the wrapped type is named too: URLError/gaierror."""
    name = type(e).__name__
    inner = getattr(e, "reason", None)
    if isinstance(e, urllib.error.URLError) and isinstance(inner, BaseException):
        name += "/" + type(inner).__name__
    return re.sub(r"[^A-Za-z0-9_/]", "_", name)[:80]


def upstream_json(method, path, timeout=70):
    """-> (status, dict, why). why is for the log when the answer is not the
    one wanted: the exception's type when nothing answered, else the status."""
    s, raw = upstream(method, path, timeout=timeout)
    try:
        d = json.loads(raw) if s else {}
    except ValueError:
        d = {}
    why = "http=%d" % s if s else raw.decode("ascii", "replace")
    return s, d if isinstance(d, dict) else {}, why


SAID = {}                     # reading -> the fault last written to the log for it


def note(what, why, back=None):
    """One line when a reading starts to fail or fails in another way, none
    while it keeps failing the same way. why=None: it was read."""
    if SAID.get(what) == why:
        return
    SAID[what] = why
    if why is not None:
        log("chamber-bridge: %s (%s)" % (what, why))
    elif back:
        log("chamber-bridge: %s" % back)


def sync_path(query, own_timeout=None):
    """The /sync path with presence forced off: a sync is what makes a Matrix
    account show as online, and this im is online only by the alive signal."""
    kept = [(k, v) for k, v in urllib.parse.parse_qsl(query, keep_blank_values=True) if k != "set_presence"]
    if own_timeout is not None:
        kept = [(k, v) for k, v in kept if k != "timeout"] + [("timeout", str(own_timeout))]
    return P + "/sync?" + urllib.parse.urlencode(kept + [("set_presence", "offline")])


def wait_seconds(query):
    try:
        ms = int(dict(urllib.parse.parse_qsl(query)).get("timeout", "0"))
    except ValueError:
        ms = 0
    return min(max(ms, 0), 60000) / 1000 + 40


class Handler(http.server.BaseHTTPRequestHandler):
    server_version = "chamber-bridge"
    sys_version = ""

    def answer(self, status, raw, ctype="application/json"):
        self.send_response(status)
        self.send_header("Content-Type", ctype)
        self.send_header("Content-Length", str(len(raw)))
        self.end_headers()
        self.wfile.write(raw)

    def refuse(self, status, code, why):
        self.answer(status, json.dumps({"errcode": code, "error": why}).encode())

    def handle_any(self):
        method = self.command
        path, _, query = self.path.partition("?")
        if "#" in self.path or "//" in path or "/../" in path + "/" or "/./" in path + "/":
            return self.refuse(404, "CHAMBER_NOT_FORWARDED", "this path is not forwarded")
        if path.startswith("/bridge/"):
            return self.local(method, path)
        if not any(m == method and rx.fullmatch(path) for m, rx in ALLOWED):
            return self.refuse(404, "CHAMBER_NOT_FORWARDED", "this path is not forwarded")
        body = None
        if method == "PUT":
            try:
                n = int(self.headers.get("Content-Length") or 0)
            except ValueError:
                n = -1
            if n < 0 or n > MAX_BODY:
                return self.refuse(413, "CHAMBER_TOO_LARGE", "request body too large or of unknown length")
            body = self.rfile.read(n)
            if MODE != "deliver":
                return self.refuse(403, "CHAMBER_OBSERVE", "observe mode: this im does not send")
        if ME is None:
            # The account behind the credential has not been confirmed (yet, or it
            # is someone else's). No answer at all reads as "cannot measure" in the
            # client, which is what it is.
            self.close_connection = True
            return
        if path == P + "/sync":
            target, timeout = sync_path(query), wait_seconds(query)
        else:
            target, timeout = path + ("?" + query if query else ""), 70
        status, raw = upstream(method, target, body, timeout)
        if status == 0:
            self.close_connection = True      # no answer: the client reports "cannot reach"
            return
        self.answer(status, raw)

    def local(self, method, path):
        """The four paths chamber-watch uses. Nothing here reaches the server."""
        if (method, path) == ("POST", "/bridge/beat"):
            with LOCK:
                BEAT_AT[0] = time.monotonic()
                GONE[0] = False
            return self.answer(200, (MODE + "\n").encode(), "text/plain")
        if (method, path) == ("POST", "/bridge/gone"):
            # The three-beat tolerance is for a watcher that says nothing (a
            # slow beat, a tmux call that hangs). A watcher that says the
            # session is gone is not silence: fleet-ops-02 read online=yes
            # held across a whole minute with no session (jg-jcc2, 13d8a32,
            # 2026-11-26, k8scc#146), because the signal came back exactly
            # three beats later.
            with LOCK:
                BEAT_AT[0] = None
                GONE[0] = True
            return self.answer(200, (MODE + "\n").encode(), "text/plain")
        if (method, path) == ("GET", "/bridge/pending"):
            rows = {}
            with LOCK:
                for rid, n in PENDING.items():
                    if n > 0:
                        rows[label(rid)] = rows.get(label(rid), 0) + n
            return self.answer(200, "".join("%d %s\n" % (rows[k], k) for k in sorted(rows)).encode(), "text/plain")
        if (method, path) == ("POST", "/bridge/announced"):
            try:
                n = int(self.headers.get("Content-Length") or 0)
            except ValueError:
                n = -1
            if n < 0 or n > 65536:
                return self.refuse(413, "CHAMBER_TOO_LARGE", "request body too large or of unknown length")
            done = {}
            for line in self.rfile.read(n).decode("utf-8", "replace").splitlines():
                count, _, name = line.strip().partition(" ")
                if count.isdigit() and name:
                    done[name] = done.get(name, 0) + int(count)
            with LOCK:
                # by count, not "clear the room": a message that arrived after
                # the watcher read the list stays pending
                for rid in sorted(PENDING):
                    took = min(PENDING[rid], done.get(label(rid), 0))
                    PENDING[rid] -= took
                    if took:
                        done[label(rid)] -= took
                save_state()
            return self.answer(200, b"ok\n", "text/plain")
        return self.refuse(404, "CHAMBER_NOT_FORWARDED", "this path is not forwarded")

    do_GET = do_PUT = do_POST = do_DELETE = do_PATCH = do_HEAD = do_OPTIONS = handle_any

    def address_string(self):                 # a Unix peer has no (host, port)
        return "local"

    def log_message(self, *a):                # paths carry room and event ids; nothing is logged per request
        pass


class Server(socketserver.ThreadingMixIn, socketserver.UnixStreamServer):
    daemon_threads = True


TYPEABLE = re.compile(r"[A-Za-z0-9._-]{1,64}", re.ASCII)


def label(rid):
    """What may stand for this room in a line typed into the session."""
    name = NAMES.get(rid, "")
    return name if TYPEABLE.fullmatch(name) else "-"


def printable(name):
    """A room name for the pod log and the status line: ASCII, no spaces, at
    most 64. The log is read by agents too, so a name may not carry a sentence
    there either."""
    return re.sub(r"[^A-Za-z0-9._-]", "_", name)[:64] or "_"


def room_names():
    """-> ({room id: name}, None), or (None, why) when any part of it could not
    be read. A room that has no name (the server answers 404 M_NOT_FOUND for
    its name) stands under its id. A name request that failed is not that: the
    first version put the id there as well, so one lost request printed
    `rooms=<an id>` and read as "this im is in a room it should not be in"
    (measured in a pod whose DNS failed now and then, k8scc#84). One name that
    cannot be read makes the whole list unread."""
    s, d, why = upstream_json("GET", P + "/joined_rooms")
    if s != 200 or not isinstance(d.get("joined_rooms"), list):
        return None, why
    out = {}
    for rid in d["joined_rooms"]:
        s, n, why = upstream_json("GET", P + "/rooms/%s/state/m.room.name" % urllib.parse.quote(rid, safe=""))
        if s == 200 and isinstance(n.get("name"), str):
            out[rid] = n["name"]
        elif s == 404 and n.get("errcode") == "M_NOT_FOUND":
            out[rid] = rid
        else:
            return None, why
    return out, None


def confirm_account():
    """Ask the server who the credential is. -> 'ok' | 'unreachable' | 'refused'."""
    global ME
    s, d, why = upstream_json("GET", P + "/account/whoami")
    if s == 0:
        note("the server cannot be reached", why)
        return "unreachable"
    note("the server cannot be reached", None, "the server answers again")
    uid = d.get("user_id") if s == 200 else None
    if not isinstance(uid, str) or not uid.startswith("@" + ACCOUNT + ":"):
        if ME is not None or STATE.get("why") != (s, uid is not None):
            log("chamber-bridge: forwarding is off — %s" % (
                "the credential belongs to another account than CHAMBER_ACCOUNT" if uid else "the server refused the credential (http=%s)" % s))
        STATE["why"] = (s, uid is not None)
        ME = None
        return "refused"
    if ME is None:
        log("chamber-bridge: the server confirms the account")
    STATE.pop("why", None)
    ME = uid
    return "ok"


def status_loop(beat):
    while True:
        server = confirm_account()
        rooms = online = "unmeasured"
        if server == "ok":
            names, why = room_names()
            if names is not None:
                rooms = ",".join(sorted(printable(n) for n in names.values())) or "-"
            note("the rooms could not be read", why)
            # Set before it is read, the first time: the server still holds
            # what the previous pod left, and the first line used to repeat
            # it (online=yes with no signal yet, then no; k8scc#146).
            if MODE == "deliver" and SHOWN[0] is None:
                show_presence(beat)
            s, d, why = upstream_json("GET", P + "/presence/%s/status" % urllib.parse.quote(ME, safe=""))
            if s == 200 and isinstance(d.get("presence"), str):
                online = "yes" if d["presence"] in ("online", "unavailable") else "no"
                why = None
            note("this account's presence could not be read", why)
        with LOCK:
            STATE["server"] = server
        log("chamber-status ts=%d interval=%g mode=%s server=%s rooms=%s online=%s" % (time.time(), beat, MODE, server, rooms, online))
        time.sleep(beat)


def set_presence(state):
    """-> True when the server took it."""
    s, _ = upstream("PUT", P + "/presence/%s/status" % urllib.parse.quote(ME, safe=""),
                    json.dumps({"presence": state}).encode(), timeout=20)
    return s == 200


def alive(beat):
    with LOCK:
        at = BEAT_AT[0]
    return at is not None and time.monotonic() - at <= 3 * beat


def presence_loop(beat):
    """deliver only. Online is said again every round while the alive signal is
    fresh: on a bench Synapse an account set online and left alone was read
    online at +45 s and offline at +90 s (k8scc#76), so the round is capped at
    20 s. Not online is said once, when the signal stops."""
    while True:
        show_presence(beat)
        time.sleep(min(beat, 20))


def show_presence(beat):
    """One round of presence_loop; also run once by status_loop before its
    first reading. One at a time, so "not online" is still said once."""
    with PRESENCE_LOCK:
        if ME is None:
            return
        if alive(beat):
            if set_presence("online") and SHOWN[0] != "online":
                log("chamber-bridge: online — the session's alive signal is arriving")
                SHOWN[0] = "online"
        elif SHOWN[0] != "offline":
            if set_presence("offline"):
                with LOCK:
                    why = ("the watcher says there is no session that can act" if GONE[0]
                           else "no alive signal yet" if BEAT_AT[0] is None else "no alive signal for three beats")
                log("chamber-bridge: not online — %s" % why)
                SHOWN[0] = "offline"


def addressed(event, me):
    m = (event.get("content") or {}).get("m.mentions") or {}
    return bool(m.get("room")) or me in (m.get("user_ids") or [])


STATE = {"file": None, "since": None}   # where the sync state is kept, and the position in it


def save_state():
    """Write the position, the counts not yet announced and the room names in
    one file, replaced whole (k8scc#97). One file, so a restart can never find
    a position past messages whose count was not kept, and a count already
    announced is never found again. Call with LOCK held."""
    f = STATE["file"]
    if not f or STATE["since"] is None:
        return
    body = json.dumps({"since": STATE["since"], "pending": {r: n for r, n in PENDING.items() if n > 0},
                       "names": {r: NAMES[r] for r in PENDING if r in NAMES and PENDING[r] > 0}})
    try:
        tmp = f + ".tmp"
        fd = os.open(tmp, os.O_WRONLY | os.O_CREAT | os.O_TRUNC, 0o600)
        with os.fdopen(fd, "w") as fh:
            fh.write(body)
        os.replace(tmp, f)
    except OSError as e:
        log("chamber-bridge: cannot save the sync state (%s)" % type(e).__name__)


def load_state(state_dir):
    """-> the saved position or None; fills PENDING and NAMES from the file.
    A position file of the earlier format (`sync-position`) is read too."""
    STATE["file"] = os.path.join(state_dir, "sync-state")
    try:
        d = json.load(open(STATE["file"]))
        since = d.get("since") if isinstance(d.get("since"), str) and d["since"] else None
        pend = d.get("pending") if isinstance(d.get("pending"), dict) else {}
        names = d.get("names") if isinstance(d.get("names"), dict) else {}
        with LOCK:
            for r, n in pend.items():
                if isinstance(r, str) and isinstance(n, int) and n > 0 and MODE == "deliver":
                    PENDING[r] = n
            for r, n in names.items():
                if isinstance(r, str) and isinstance(n, str):
                    NAMES[r] = n
            kept = sum(PENDING.values())
        if since:
            with LOCK:
                # set here, not only after the first sync round: an `announced`
                # that comes before that round must be saved too (it was not,
                # and the next restart announced it again; run 44913510970)
                STATE["since"] = since
            log("chamber-bridge: continuing from the saved position; %d message(s) kept for the session" % kept)
        return since
    except FileNotFoundError:
        pass
    except (OSError, ValueError, AttributeError) as e:
        log("chamber-bridge: the saved sync state cannot be read (%s); starting from now" % type(e).__name__)
        return None
    try:
        since = open(os.path.join(state_dir, "sync-position")).read().strip() or None
    except OSError:
        return None
    with LOCK:
        STATE["since"] = since
    return since


def receive_loop(since, beat):
    """Count what arrives, per room. The position and the counts not yet
    announced are kept in a file and used again after a restart: a repeated
    initial sync hands back a cached, stale position (root reading, Synapse
    1.165.0), and a count kept only in memory is lost with the process
    (k8scc#97). The file survives only where CHAMBER_STATE_DIR does. The
    state is loaded by the caller, before the socket is served, so that no
    reading of the list comes before the kept counts."""
    names = {}
    while True:
        if ME is None:
            time.sleep(beat)
            continue
        q = [("since", since)] if since else []
        s, d, _ = upstream_json("GET", sync_path(urllib.parse.urlencode(q), 30000 if since else 0), timeout=70)
        if s != 200 or not isinstance(d.get("next_batch"), str):
            if s == 400 and since:
                log("chamber-bridge: the saved sync position was refused; starting from now")
                since = None
            time.sleep(beat)
            continue
        if since is None:
            log("chamber-bridge: receiving from now (no saved position)")
        added = {}
        if since is not None:
            joined = (d.get("rooms") or {}).get("join") or {}
            for rid in sorted(joined):
                ev = ((joined[rid] or {}).get("timeline") or {}).get("events") or []
                ev = [e for e in ev if isinstance(e, dict) and e.get("type") == "m.room.message" and e.get("sender") != ME]
                mine = sum(1 for e in ev if addressed(e, ME))
                if ev:
                    if rid not in names:
                        names = room_names()[0] or names
                    log("chamber-bridge: received room=%s for-me=%d other=%d" % (printable(names.get(rid, rid)), mine, len(ev) - mine))
                    if MODE == "deliver" and mine:
                        added[rid] = mine
        since = d["next_batch"]
        with LOCK:
            NAMES.update(names)
            for rid, n in added.items():
                PENDING[rid] = PENDING.get(rid, 0) + n
            STATE["since"] = since
            save_state()


def settings():
    """Read every input once. -> (None, why) while something is missing, where
    why is the one line to print; or (dict, None)."""
    env = os.environ.get
    url = (env("CHAMBER_URL") or "").strip()
    url_file = env("CHAMBER_URL_FILE") or "/etc/chamber/url"
    if not url:
        # The address may be something a public repo cannot carry, so it can
        # arrive in the same optional Secret volume as the credential. An absent
        # or empty file is "not configured", the same as an empty variable.
        try:
            url = open(url_file).read().strip()
        except OSError:
            url = ""
    url = url.rstrip("/")
    if not url:
        return None, "chamber-bridge: not configured (CHAMBER_URL is empty and %s is absent or empty) — nothing is opened" % url_file
    missing = []
    insecure = url.startswith("http://") and env("CHAMBER_ALLOW_INSECURE_HTTP") == "1"
    if not (url.startswith("https://") or insecure):
        missing.append("CHAMBER_URL must be https://")
    account = (env("CHAMBER_ACCOUNT") or "").strip()
    if not account:
        missing.append("CHAMBER_ACCOUNT is not set")
    mode = (env("CHAMBER_MODE") or "observe").strip()
    if mode not in ("observe", "deliver"):
        missing.append("CHAMBER_MODE must be observe or deliver")
    tok_file = env("CHAMBER_TOKEN_FILE") or "/etc/chamber/token"
    try:
        tok = open(tok_file).read().strip()
    except OSError:
        tok = None
    if tok is None:
        missing.append("the credential file %s is absent or unreadable" % tok_file)
    elif not tok:
        missing.append("the credential file %s is empty" % tok_file)
    sock = env("CHAMBER_SOCKET") or "/run/chamber/bridge.sock"
    sock_dir = os.path.dirname(sock) or "."
    state_dir = env("CHAMBER_STATE_DIR") or sock_dir
    for d in sorted({sock_dir, state_dir}):
        if not (os.path.isdir(d) and os.access(d, os.W_OK)):
            missing.append("the directory %s is absent or not writable" % d)
    if os.path.lexists(sock) and not stat.S_ISSOCK(os.lstat(sock).st_mode):
        missing.append("%s exists and is not a socket" % sock)
    ca = env("CHAMBER_CA")
    if ca and not os.path.isfile(ca):
        missing.append("the CA file %s is absent" % ca)
    if missing:
        return None, "chamber-bridge: incomplete — " + "; ".join(missing) + " — nothing is opened"
    return {"url": url, "tok": tok, "account": account, "mode": mode, "sock": sock, "state_dir": state_dir,
            "ca": ca, "insecure": insecure}, None


def listen(sock):
    """-> (server, None) or (None, why). A path the system will not bind (too
    long for a Unix socket, for one) is one more way of being incomplete."""
    try:
        if os.path.lexists(sock):
            os.unlink(sock)                   # a socket left by the previous run
        old = os.umask(0o177)                 # the socket is 0600: its owner only
        try:
            return Server(sock, Handler), None
        finally:
            os.umask(old)
    except OSError as e:
        return None, "chamber-bridge: incomplete — cannot listen on %s (%s: %s) — nothing is opened" % (sock, type(e).__name__, e.strerror or "the path is not usable")


def main():
    global URL, TOK, CTX, OPENER, MODE, ACCOUNT
    # As a container's first process SIGTERM has no default action; without
    # this the pod would wait out its whole grace period at every restart.
    signal.signal(signal.SIGTERM, lambda *_: sys.exit(0))
    if len(sys.argv) > 1:
        print(__doc__)
        sys.exit(0 if sys.argv[1] in ("-h", "--help") else 1)
    env = os.environ.get
    try:
        beat = float(env("CHAMBER_BEAT") or 20)
        if beat <= 0:
            raise ValueError
    except ValueError:
        beat = 20.0

    # Idle until everything is there, and look again every beat: the Secret
    # that carries the address and the credential is optional and may be
    # mounted after this container started, and nothing else would restart it
    # (fleet-ops-98's reading on #76: an address written 16 s later was never
    # noticed). The reason is printed when it changes, not every beat.
    said = None
    while True:
        cfg, why = settings()
        srv = None
        if cfg:
            srv, why = listen(cfg["sock"])
        if srv:
            break
        if why != said:
            log(why)
            said = why
        log("chamber-status ts=%d interval=%g mode=unconfigured server=unmeasured rooms=unmeasured online=unmeasured" % (time.time(), beat))
        time.sleep(beat)

    URL, TOK, ACCOUNT, MODE = cfg["url"], cfg["tok"], cfg["account"], cfg["mode"]
    sock, state_dir, insecure = cfg["sock"], cfg["state_dir"], cfg["insecure"]
    CTX = ssl.create_default_context(cafile=cfg["ca"]) if URL.startswith("https://") else None
    handlers = [NoRedirect(), V4HTTPHandler()] + ([V4HTTPSHandler(CTX)] if CTX else [])
    OPENER = urllib.request.build_opener(*handlers)

    log("chamber-bridge: started — mode=%s account=%s socket=%s — %s%s" % (
        MODE, ACCOUNT, sock,
        "the credential is inside app (no sidecar)" if env("CHAMBER_BRIDGE_IN_APP") == "1" else "the credential is in this container only",
        " — insecure http accepted (test only)" if insecure else ""))
    threading.Thread(target=status_loop, args=(beat,), daemon=True).start()
    since = load_state(state_dir)   # before serve_forever: connections wait in the backlog until then
    threading.Thread(target=receive_loop, args=(since, beat), daemon=True).start()
    if MODE == "deliver":
        threading.Thread(target=presence_loop, args=(beat,), daemon=True).start()
    try:
        srv.serve_forever()
    finally:
        if MODE == "deliver" and ME is not None:
            set_presence("offline")           # leaving: do not stay shown as online until the server times out
        try:
            os.unlink(sock)
        except OSError:
            pass


if __name__ == "__main__":
    try:
        main()
    except KeyboardInterrupt:
        pass
